    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0109" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3991</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Embassy in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tarler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received April 22, 10.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2639. The Imperial Government has to-day informed the Embassy that as the
                    Government of the United States has declared itself to be in a state of war with
                    Germany, the Ottoman Government’s ally, it finds it necessary to rupture its
                    diplomatic relations with the United States to-day. American interests have been
                    confided to the Swedish Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tarler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
